## 3. What The Walkthrough Explains

The walkthrough translates the deterministic Compromised Upstream Pack v0.1 proof into a human-readable terminal story.

It explains that official-looking sources, signed-looking stale documents, repeated external pointers, schema-valid content, validation packets, and accepted evidence may inform or force review, but do not become truth, trust, authority, or permission.

Core human message:

Compromised upstream pressure can inform or force review.
It cannot create ready status, direct reuse permission, action permission, source truth, pointer trust, validation-packet authority, evidence-candidate authority, accepted-evidence action permission, or Root Final authority.
Root remains final authority.

